@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Azure Monitor & Application Insights";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Azure Monitor and Application Insights provide powerful monitoring capabilities that help DevOps teams track application health, diagnose issues, and optimize performance.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>What is Azure Monitor?</h2>
        <p>Azure Monitor is a comprehensive monitoring solution that collects, analyzes, and acts on telemetry data from applications, infrastructure, and network resources.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Collects Metrics & Logs:</strong> Gathers performance and diagnostic data from Azure services.</li>
            <li><strong>Enables Real-Time Alerts:</strong> Detects anomalies and triggers alerts based on predefined conditions.</li>
            <li><strong>Supports Custom Dashboards:</strong> Visualizes data using customizable dashboards in Azure Portal.</li>
            <li><strong>Integrates with Third-Party Tools:</strong> Works with Grafana, Splunk, and other monitoring solutions.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-4">
        <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/monitoring/media/monitoring-overview.png" alt="Azure Monitor Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
        <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Monitor Dashboard</small></p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>What is Application Insights?</h2>
        <p>Application Insights is an Application Performance Monitoring (APM) tool that helps detect, diagnose, and optimize application performance.</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Detects Performance Issues:</strong> Tracks response times, failures, and bottlenecks in applications.</li>
            <li><strong>Provides End-to-End Transaction Tracing:</strong> Captures telemetry across multiple components.</li>
            <li><strong>Analyzes User Behavior:</strong> Offers insights into user interactions and session patterns.</li>
            <li><strong>Supports Multiple Platforms:</strong> Works with .NET, Java, Node.js, Python, and other frameworks.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-4">
        <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/monitoring/media/application-insights-overview.png" alt="Application Insights Dashboard" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
        <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Application Insights Dashboard</small></p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Setting Up Azure Monitor & Application Insights</h3>
        <p>Follow these steps to enable monitoring for your applications:</p>
        <ol>
            <li><strong>Enable Azure Monitor:</strong> Go to Azure Portal > Monitor > Create a monitoring workspace.</li>
            <li><strong>Add Application Insights:</strong> Install the SDK and configure telemetry collection.</li>
            <li><strong>Set Up Log Analytics:</strong> Connect Azure resources for centralized log collection.</li>
            <li><strong>Define Alert Rules:</strong> Configure notifications for performance thresholds.</li>
            <li><strong>Create Dashboards:</strong> Use Azure Monitor Workbooks to visualize key performance indicators.</li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Example YAML for Monitoring Integration</h3>
        <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded">
steps:
- task: AzureMonitorAlerts@1
  inputs:
    azureSubscription: 'MyAzureSubscription'
    resourceGroupName: 'MyResourceGroup'
    alertRuleName: 'HighCPUAlert'
    conditionOperator: 'GreaterThan'
    conditionThreshold: '80'
        </pre>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Best Practices for Using Azure Monitor & Application Insights</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Enable Distributed Tracing:</strong> Link telemetry across microservices for better debugging.</li>
            <li><strong>Monitor User Experience:</strong> Use Application Insights to analyze real user sessions.</li>
            <li><strong>Automate Alerts & Scaling:</strong> Set up auto-scaling based on real-time metrics.</li>
            <li><strong>Leverage AI Insights:</strong> Use Azure’s AI-powered anomaly detection for proactive monitoring.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <p>Azure Monitor and Application Insights provide comprehensive monitoring, helping DevOps teams ensure application stability, detect issues, and optimize performance.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("IntroMonitoringDevOps", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: Introduction to Monitoring in DevOps</a>
        <a href="@Url.Action("LogAnalyticsAlerts", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next: Log Analytics & Alerts &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>